arding **T2** leaves T3-T3-T4-T5, which can form [T3,T4,T5] + T3 waiting.\n\nReason:\n\nDiscarding **T2** optimizes my hand structure because:\n1. It's relatively isolated in the Bamboo sequence\n2. Keeps the complete W3-W4-W5 chow intact\n3. Maintains T3-T3-T4-T5 which can form [T3,T4,T5] chow with T3 remaining flexible\n4. Preserves the valuable B2-B2-B3-B3-B4-B4 structure which offers multiple winning possibilities\n5. With 3 T2s still unshown but my hand becoming more structured toward Bamboo tiles for melds, T2 is the least useful\n\nAnswer: Play T2"}
